    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 0.44,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.12,
    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot by several factors and scaled each reading back up. Dilution 2 gave 0.2266, which scales to 0.453. Dilution 3 gave 0.1601, which scales to 0.480. Dilution 5 gave 0.082, which scales to 0.41. Dilution 10 gave 0.0432 (two reads), which scales to 0.43. The undiluted reading is about 0.42. The scaled values do not rise steadily with dilution, as they would if the reader were saturating at high density. They scatter around 0.41–0.48, and the low-OD reads carry roughly 10% noise. The plateau at about 0.42 is therefore real stationary-phase biomass and not a detector ceiling. The scaled mean is about 0.44, only slightly above the undiluted reading and within noise."
